.TH PESTUDIO 1 "August 2026" "vst-ace" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pestudio \- browse and play audio plug\-ins natively, with their own editors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pestudio
.RI [ dir | bank.json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pestudio
is a Qt6 plug\-in browser and player. Pick a folder, pick a plug\-in, and it
gives you the plug\-in's programs, every exposed parameter, a playable
keyboard, a pitch wheel, patch banks, a recorder, and the plug\-in's own editor
\(em drawn into a buffer and blitted for Windows plug\-ins, embedded as an X11
child window for native Linux ones.
.PP
Plug\-ins built for Windows, macOS and Linux all load as native code; there is
no Wine and no emulation. They are hosted out of process by default, so one
that faults costs a helper rather than the session.
.PP
The \fBShow: Instruments / Effects\fR boxes above the list narrow it to one
kind. Each plug\-in is checked once, in the background, and the answer is kept
in \fI~/.cache/vst\-ace/plugin\-roles\fR.
.PP
Given a directory it browses that; given a bank it opens the plug\-ins the bank
names with their patches loaded. With neither, it starts on the corpus named by
.BR VST_ROOT ,
or
.I ~/vst
when that is unset.
.PP
Launching it as
.B va pe
sets the X11 backend first, which is what a plug\-in's own editor needs; see
.BR va (1).
.SH CONNECT MENU
.TP
.B Connect to REAPER
Wires this synth to REAPER: its audio into the next free pair of REAPER's
inputs, and the next free REAPER MIDI output into the synth. Several pestudio
windows can be connected at once. Start REAPER with \fBpw\-jack reaper\fR.
.TP
.B Show in DAWs' FX list
Puts the loaded plug\-in in \fI~/.vst\fR (or \fI~/.vst3\fR) so REAPER or any
other DAW can add it to a track. Rescan plug\-ins in the DAW afterwards. Untick
to take it out. Each start of pestudio updates these copies to the current
build. Not available in the AppImage.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM
Editors embed through an X11 window id, so this wants to be \fBxcb\fR under
Wayland; XWayland is enough. Override it for a native Wayland window and no
native editors.
.TP
.B VST_ROOT
The plug\-in corpus to start on.
.TP
.B PEHOST_ISOLATE
Set to 0 to host in process rather than behind the helper.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR va (1),
.BR peload (1),
.BR dwstudio (1).
